<!-- The Android TV banner (android:banner): the mark and wordmark from
     assets/banners/ks_banner_light.svg on #F5F4F2 (the remote
     admin's light background token), with Kiosk in
     #3a3a3a and Satellite in #5c5c5c, fitted
     into the 16:9 field TV homes draw instead of the square icon. The
     lockup is restacked for the field: no "for Home Assistant" subline
     and Satellite under Kiosk, so the glyphs run about twice the height
     the wide lockup would allow. A vector rather than the 320x180 PNG
     the platform docs describe so the lockup stays sharp on a home that
     scales it, and so no second copy of the artwork ships. Declared at
     twice the 160x90dp the platform describes, with the same viewport,
     because the stock TV home rasterizes the drawable at its intrinsic
     size and scales that bitmap to its card: at 1x small glyphs came out
     soft on a Shield, and at 4x the near sevenfold downscale smeared
     them. 2x is the bitmap YouTube's own 320x180 PNG decodes to on an
     xhdpi box, and that card is the reference. Generated from the SVG by
     a one-off script;
     regenerate from the SVG rather than editing the paths here. -->
